  "request": "GitHub Issue #439 Pass same-spec contract context to impl-gate preservation evaluation. Goal: Pass each impl-gate requirement evaluation a bounded authoritative same-spec context containing the current requirement full text, ID-keyed summaries of same-spec requirements, migration or contract replacement decisions, and clarifications affecting legacy input or output validity, so preservation is evaluated against the current contract. Validate that an R6-equivalent case from #437 passes with the R1/R2 replacement and legacy [] invalidation, while a real violation of the new required enum contract fails. Bounds: requirement summaries 64 items/768 chars, decisions 24 items/1024 chars, clarifications 24 items/1024 chars, total 48000 chars, deterministic item-boundary truncation and fixed truncation records, no new agent call. Scope: src/flow/lib/run-gate.js, impl-gate prompt/context construction, preservation guidance, focused deterministic and regression tests. Out of scope per #436 boundary: AC/task/implementationTargets/file-map/evidence/full schema/design/data-flow/obligation classification/full architecture, output finding contract redesign, global citation changes, retry architecture, branch repair. Preserve existing output schema, cache identity except legitimate prompt input change, semantic counters, retry policy, artifacts, routing, and all non-impl gates. Constraints: Node built-ins only, generic src, OOP invariants, alpha no compatibility fallback, no test changes merely to force pass.",
